---
[v1] net: phy: sfp: make mod-def0 GPIO shareable for combo SFP/PHY
designs

Add GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE flag to mod-def0 GPIO to allow sharing
between SFP module detection and passive mux control.
---
v1: make mod-def0 GPIO shareable for combo SFP/PHY designs
---

From 8bbccf7263fb6bd902baef5c15e9472b58b79fd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "neal.yen" <neal.yen@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Oct 2025 10:57:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: sfp: add shared capability to mod-def0 gpio

The combo SFP/PHY dynamic switching through the passive mux will use the
mod-def0 GPIO to detect whether the SFP module has been inserted.
We need to change this GPIO to shared to avoid failures in GPIO
requests within mtk_add_mux().

Also request the module GPIO interrupts with IRQF_SHARED.
ledtrig-gpio holds the shared lines' IRQs with IRQF_SHARED, so the
sfp driver's non-shared request failed with -EBUSY (genirq flags
mismatch) and the sfp core fell back to 1-second polling.

Signed-off-by: neal.yen <neal.yen@mediatek.com>

--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -158,9 +158,9 @@ static const char *gpio_names[] = {
 };
 
 static const enum gpiod_flags gpio_flags[] = {
-	GPIOD_IN,
-	GPIOD_IN,
-	GPIOD_IN,
+	GPIOD_IN | GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE,	/* mod-def0 */
+	GPIOD_IN | GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE,	/* los      */
+	GPIOD_IN | GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE,	/* tx-fault */
 	GPIOD_ASIS,
 	GPIOD_ASIS,
 	GPIOD_ASIS,
@@ -836,7 +836,7 @@ static unsigned int sfp_gpio_get_state(s
 	unsigned int i, state, v;
 
 	for (i = state = 0; i < GPIO_MAX; i++) {
-		if (gpio_flags[i] != GPIOD_IN || !sfp->gpio[i])
+		if ((gpio_flags[i] & GPIOD_IN) != GPIOD_IN || !sfp->gpio[i])
 			continue;
 
 		v = gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[i]);
@@ -3468,7 +3468,7 @@ static int sfp_probe(struct platform_dev
 	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < GPIO_MAX; i++) {
-		if (gpio_flags[i] != GPIOD_IN || !sfp->gpio[i])
+		if ((gpio_flags[i] & GPIOD_IN) != GPIOD_IN || !sfp->gpio[i])
 			continue;
 
 		sfp->gpio_irq[i] = gpiod_to_irq(sfp->gpio[i]);
@@ -3485,9 +3485,16 @@ static int sfp_probe(struct platform_dev
 		if (!sfp_irq_name)
 			return -ENOMEM;
 
+		/* The module GPIOs may be shared with gpio-triggered LEDs
+		 * (ledtrig-gpio requests the lines with IRQF_SHARED); request
+		 * the interrupt shared as well so both consumers get events
+		 * instead of this one failing with -EBUSY and falling back
+		 * to polling.
+		 */
 		err = devm_request_threaded_irq(sfp->dev, sfp->gpio_irq[i],
 						NULL, sfp_irq,
 						IRQF_ONESHOT |
+						IRQF_SHARED |
 						IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING |
 						IRQF_TRIGGER_FALLING,
 						sfp_irq_name, sfp);
